  "worked_solution": "Let $A$ denote the area under the curve $y=r(t)$ over $[0,6].$ In this case, we have $n=2$ rectangles. Using the right Riemann sum, the area is computed as \n\n$$\nA\u2248r(2)\u0394{t}_{1}+r(6)\u0394{t}_{2},\n$$\n\nwhere each $\u0394{t}_{i}$ is calculated by considering the step between a particular $t$-value and the previous one, i.e.,\n\n$$\n\u0394{t}_{i}={t}_{i}-{t}_{i-1}.\n$$\n\nWe set up a value table that includes the $\u0394t$'s.\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\u0394t$ | $-$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| $r(t)$ | $-$ | $2$ | $1$ |\n\nWe plug in the numbers to approximate the area under the curve and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & \u22482\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =4+4 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, in the given context, the area under the curve represents the total accumulation of emissions. So, the total carbon dioxide emitted is $8$ tons.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
